Invented by Johannes Gutenberg around 1440 in Mainz, Germany, the movable type printing press revolutionized the spread of information and permanently altered the course of human history. By mechanizing the process of printing, Gutenberg’s invention drastically reduced the cost and time required to produce books, making knowledge accessible to a broader audience beyond the elite and clergy. This technological breakthrough fueled the Renaissance, the Reformation, and the Scientific Revolution, effectively democratizing literacy
